WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
The reasoning era.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:06.060
Since twenty twenty-four, models learned to think before answering.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.767
These twelve terms cover that shift, and the prompting patterns that came before.

4
00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:19.467
Reasoning models are trained, largely with reinforcement learning, to produce long internal chains of thought before answering.

5
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:25.833
Think OpenAI's o-series, DeepSeek-R1, Gemini thinking modes, and Claude extended thinking.

6
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:30.700
They're much better at math, code, and planning, but slower and pricier per query.

7
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.867
Test-time compute is the scaling law of the moment.

8
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:43.800
Instead of only training bigger models, you spend more compute at inference, with longer thinking, multiple samples, or search, to buy accuracy.

9
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.267
It's also called inference-time scaling.

10
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:51.700
Chain-of-thought prompts the model to reason step by step before answering.

11
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.400
It's the single most cited prompting technique.

12
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.633
Reasoning models internalized it.

13
00:00:57.833 --> 00:01:03.233
Tree and graph of thoughts explore multiple reasoning branches, evaluate them, and backtrack.

14
00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:06.500
It's a search over thoughts instead of one linear chain.

15
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:12.300
Mostly research vocabulary, but the idea reappears inside reasoning-model training.

16
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:21.067
Self-consistency samples the same question several times at nonzero temperature, then majority-votes the answers.

17
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:26.133
It's a crude but effective accuracy boost, and an ancestor of test-time compute.

18
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:32.633
Chain-of-draft has the model reason in terse, abbreviated notes instead of full prose.

19
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:37.421
You get near chain-of-thought accuracy at a fraction of the tokens.

20
00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:40.033
It's a cost-optimization flavor of CoT.

21
00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:47.833
In-context learning means the model learns a task purely from examples in the prompt, with no weight updates.

22
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:51.033
That's the phenomenon that makes few-shot prompting work.

23
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:55.667
Zero-shot is the opposite end: instructions only, no examples.

24
00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:59.033
This one is borrowed from psychology.

25
00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:04.300
System one is fast pattern-matching, and system two is slow, deliberate reasoning.

26
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.667
It's the framing everyone uses to describe what reasoning models add.

27
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:13.133
Reflexion is the research pattern behind reflection.

28
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:17.833
The agent turns a failure into verbal self-feedback and stores it in memory.

29
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.100
On the next attempt, it does better.

30
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:27.067
In Self-Ask, the model explicitly asks and answers sub-questions before the final answer.

31
00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:34.633
In step-back prompting, you first ask a more general question, like what principles apply here, and only then the specific one.

32
00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:40.100
Prompt chaining splits a task into several sequential LLM calls.

33
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.467
Say, extract, then transform, then format, each output feeding the next input.

34
00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:51.133
It's more reliable and debuggable than one mega-prompt, and the seed of pipelines and agents.

35
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:56.421
Prompt compression shrinks long prompts while preserving their meaning.

36
00:02:56.421 --> 00:02:58.033
LLMLingua is the known tool.

37
00:02:58.333 --> 00:03:00.757
That means fewer tokens and lower cost.

38
00:03:00.757 --> 00:03:03.367
It's a niche cousin of context management.

39
00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:05.533
Let's recap.

40
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:09.767
Reasoning models spend test-time compute to think before answering.

41
00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:14.633
Chain-of-thought, self-consistency, and thought trees were the prompting ancestors.

42
00:03:14.933 --> 00:03:21.133
In-context learning powers few-shot prompting, and chaining and compression keep things reliable and cheap.
